warning[NK1308]: `tmp` reaches the path `fs::write` opens under `fs::Root::Anywhere`, which may name any file, and it comes from outside the program.
   --> tests/rt_the_blocking_path_reads_what_the_completion_path_reads.nika:26:2
    |
 26 | 	fs::write(f"{tmp}/cities.txt", fs::Root::Anywhere, "Hamburg;12.0\n".repeat(10000))
    |  ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
    |
    = note: `tmp` comes from `process::run`: whoever sends it chooses the value, so nothing the compiler can see says what it holds.
    = note: A path from outside may name any file the program can reach: `../`, or one that starts at `/`.
    = note: `raw-sinks = "warn"` lets this build through.
    = help: Open it under a root the program chose, where it cannot leave the directory: `fs::Root::Dir(".")`, `fs::scratch()` or `root.join(...)` of one. Or check it where it arrives, `throw BadInput(tmp) if !path::is_component(tmp)` (or `path::is_below`), and open it under such a root or joined to a part that is not outside. If the program means to write paths from `process`, `untrusted-paths-write = ["process"]` under `[allow]` in the manifest builds it.
